\item \points{3h} \textbf{Writeup}

If you adjust \texttt{lr}, the learning rate, how do you expect loss and validation accuracy to change
during training? Run the terminal command \texttt{python submission.py --model linear --lr [your\_learning\_rate]}
to experiment with three different learning rates. Report what they are and what training behaviors
you observed. Why did the learning rate affect loss and accuracy this way?

For example, you can run: \texttt{python submission.py --model linear --lr 0.1}.  If you don't include an \texttt{--lr} argument, the default learning rate is 0.2.

\expect{In 2-3 sentences, report three different \texttt{lr}'s you experimented with, and describe how they affected training behaviors. Explain why the learning rate affects loss and accuracy this way.}

